<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7501" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνασσα</span></b>  (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝάνασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Inscr.Cypr.</u>
					101
				</span></i>
			 H., al.), ἡ, fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ,</span>
			<i>queen, lady,</i> addressed to goddesses, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.380
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.175
			</span></i>; esp. in 
				Att.
			to Athena, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				228
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				235
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				443
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> to a
			mortal, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.149
			</span></i>, etc.—Common in Poetry from <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> downwds.; rare in Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				9.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				526
			</span></i>: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέροισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.862
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> generally, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ</span>
			 IV, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνασσα πράγους καὶ βουλεύματος</span>
			<i>authoress</i> of this deed, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				704
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					387
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <i>royal,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. βουλή,</span> of the Roman Senate, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1389i34
			</span></i>.</div>
